1
00:00:00,371 --> 00:00:03,861
(Sheldon:)...with a story about
a great female scientist.

2
00:00:04,041 --> 00:00:07,671
(Sheldon:)Polish-born, French-educated...

3
00:00:07,845 --> 00:00:08,865
(Sheldon:)...Madame Curie.

4
00:00:09,246 --> 00:00:11,736
(Sheldon:)Co-discoverer of radioactivity...

5
00:00:11,949 --> 00:00:16,579
(Sheldon:)...she was a hero of science.
Until her hair fell out...

6
00:00:16,754 --> 00:00:19,844
(Sheldon:)...her vomit and stool
became filled with blood...

7
00:00:20,991 --> 00:00:24,221
(Sheldon:)...and she was poisoned to death
by her own discovery.

8
00:00:25,896 --> 00:00:28,156
(Sheldon:)With a little hard work...

9
00:00:28,332 --> 00:00:31,892
(Sheldon:)...I see no reason
why that can't happen to any of you.

10
00:00:35,372 --> 00:00:37,502
(Sheldon:)Are we done? Can we go?

11
00:00:42,613 --> 00:00:46,573
(Howard:)The thing to remember is
you can go to outer space too.

12
00:00:46,751 --> 00:00:48,721
Heh. I mean, look at me.

13
00:00:48,886 --> 00:00:53,256
(Howard:)I went to this very school.
Those desks you're sitting in?

14
00:00:53,424 --> 00:00:55,854
(Howard:)I was once superglued to one of them.

15
00:00:57,728 --> 00:00:58,748
Mm-hm.

16
00:00:58,929 --> 00:01:00,359
(Girl:)Did you go to the moon?

